{
  "applicable": true,
  "kind": "rewrite",
  "rule": "robin_bc",
  "note": "Robin ghost rewrite at xmin (esd-6k1, supersedes the esd-6g4.8/G9 infeasibility verdict). Fires through the ESS rule engine via the fn/dim BC-kind matcher (ess-bps/ess-tox, G8) plus the makearray-region BC lowering (ess-hjg): `_discretize_bc!` encodes the BC kind->fn, side->dim, variable->arg, and the three Robin coefficients ride as trailing args [$u, $a, $b, $g] (α, β, γ). The `where` clause binds $gr = u's grid (var_has_grid) and $h = 1/N for that side's spatial dim (bind_side_spacing). Grid g1 has spatial_dims=[x], dim_sizes={x:4}, so xmin -> axis 1 -> dim x -> N=4 -> h=0.25. Coefficients are carried SYMBOLICALLY (α=a, β=b, γ=g) so the golden pins the full Robin structure with the $h=0.25 binding visible. Ghost formula: u_ghost = (2·h·γ + (2·β - α·h)·u[0]) / (α·h + 2·β) = (2·0.25·g + (2·b - a·0.25)·index(u,0)) / (a·0.25 + 2·b). The LOCAL 0-based index(u,0) is re-indexed into the grid frame per side by ess-hjg (min: u[1]; max: u[N]). This Layer-A rewrite UNIT pins that the declarative rule fires; the numeric INTEGRATION path is exercised by test/test_bc_ic_goldens.jl (bc_robin_1d.esm).",
  "context": {
    "grids": {
      "g1": { "spatial_dims": ["x"], "dim_sizes": { "x": 4 } }
    },
    "variables": {
      "u": { "grid": "g1" }
    }
  },
  "expression": {
    "op": "bc",
    "fn": "robin",
    "dim": "xmin",
    "args": ["u", "a", "b", "g"]
  }
}
